  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For a reversible&nbsp;reaction, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8652;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>,&nbsp;which one of the following statement is wrong from the given energy&nbsp;profile diagram?</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0011_f73f76e3a612.png\" style=\"width: 593px; height: 397px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Activation energy of forward reaction is greater than backward reaction",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The forward reaction is endothermic",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The threshold energy is less than that of activation energy",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "The energy of activation of forward reaction is equal to the sum of heat of reaction and the energy of activation of backward reaction",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\qt0011_f73f76e3a612.png\" style=\"width: 593px; height: 397px;\" /></p><p>where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo></math> activation energy of forward reaction</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo></math> activation energy of backward reaction</p><p>The above energy profile diagram shows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></math></p><p>The potential energy of the product is greater than that of the reactant, so the reaction is endothermic.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>&#916;E</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></math></p>"
  }
